            <ArticleTitle>Anesthesia for patients with subglottic cysts.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>209-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.478</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acquired subglottic cysts can cause rapid development of respiratory distress. Subglottic cysts are a disease of premature infants and other pathologies of prematurity should be anticipated. Perioperative success is dependent on communication between surgeon and anesthesiologist. Contingency plans for an emergency surgical airway should be in place in the event of total airway obstruction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
